    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrTab">HDR</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrHelp">Display Manager owns HDR when installed. On exit it writes the desired state — it does not trust Windows’ own HDR readout.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrPolicyTitle">Global HDR policy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrPolicyHelp">Default for every game. Per-game overrides in the game context menu always win.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrPolicyNone">Let Windows manage HDR as configured</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrPolicyAllGames">Turn HDR on when a game launches and off when it closes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrPolicyMetadata">Turn HDR on when launching a game whose metadata indicates HDR, and off when it closes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrMetadataTitle">HDR metadata match names</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrMetadataHelp">Comma-separated Feature names (case-insensitive). Works with PCGamingWiki Metadata Provider’s HDR feature. No network on launch.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrIncludeTags">Also look in game Tags</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrOverrideCountFormat">{0} game(s) with an HDR override (not inherit).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrGameMenuHint">Set overrides from the game context menu: Display Manager → HDR.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrForceSdrTitle">Force HDR off</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrForceSdrHelp">If the picture still looks like HDR after a game (glowing or washed-out desktop), use this to force a normal SDR picture. Tip: Win+Alt+B also toggles HDR so you can check by eye.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_HdrWriteOffNow">Turn HDR off on my displays</sys:String>
