    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardWelcomeTitle">Welcome</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardWelcomeHelp">Display Manager owns Windows HDR for your library when installed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardWelcomeBody">It writes HDR on/off by policy (and per-game overrides), then writes the desired exit state — it does not trust ACM readback. Playnite’s native “Enable HDR Support” checkbox can stay visible; Display Manager clears that flag so two restores do not fight.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationTitle">Clear native HDR flags?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationIntro">One-shot migration across your library. You can reverse it later from Maintenance.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationCountFormat">{0} game(s) currently have EnableSystemHdr on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardClearNative">Clear EnableSystemHdr on all those games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationHelp">If someone turns the native checkbox back on later, Display Manager clears it again on the next launch (and notifies once).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardSummaryTitle">Review and save</sys:String>
